//컴� Global variables 컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴

global struct mouse[0]
        x               // Mouse X coordinate
        y               // Mouse Y coordinate
        z               // Graphic print priority
        file            // File containing the graphic
        graph           // Graphic assigned to the mouse
        angle           // Pointer angle
        size            // Size as a percentage
        flags           // Mouse flags
        region          // Clipping region
        left            // Left mouse button
        middle          // Middle mouse button
        right           // Right mouse button
        cursor          // Emulation with cursor keys (0/1)
        speed           // Mouse speed (0..9)
end

global struct scroll[9]
        z               // Print priority
        camera          // Id of the process followed by the scroll (default 0-n/a)
        ratio           // Background speed ratio (default 200, half of the first one)
        speed           // Maximum scroll speed (foreground) (default 0-No limit)
        region1         // Scroll lock region (default -1)
        region2         // Outer scroll region (no maximum speed, default -1)
        x0              // Coordinates of the scroll foreground
        y0              // (top left corner of the window)
        x1              // Coordinates of the background
        y1              // (background plane, if any)
end

global struct m7[9]
        z               // Print priority
        camera          // Id of the process followed by the camera
        height          // Camera height
        distance        // Distance from the camera to the followed process
        horizon         // Horizon height
        focus           // Camera focal length (0..512)
        color           // Color for the outside of mode-7
end

global struct joy[0]
        button1
        button2
        button3
        button4
        left
        right
        up
        down
end

global struct setup[0]
        card
        port
        irq
        dma
        dma2
        master
        sound_fx
        cd_audio
        mixer
        rate
        bits
end

global struct net[0]
        device          // 1-IPX, 2-Serial, 3-Modem
        com             // 1..4 (serial and modem)
        speed           // Up to 115000 (serial and modem)
        number          // Phone number (modem) e.g. net.number="913040622"
        init            // Modem init string. e.g. net.init="ATZ"
        mode            // 0-1 depending on pulse or tone (modem)
        server          // Tells whether it is the server (do not touch)
        max_players     // Maximum number of players (2..16)
        num_players     // Current number of players (2..16)
end

global struct m8[9]
        z               // Print priority
        camera          // Id of the process followed by the camera
        height          // Height of the camera relative to the process
        angle           // Camera up - down angle (-128,128)
end

global struct dirinfo[0]
        files           // Number of files in the list
        name[1024]      // Names of the files
end

global struct fileinfo[0]
        string fullpath[254] // Full name
        drive           // Disk drive (1-A, 2-B, ...)
        string dir[254] // Directory
        string name[7]  // Name
        string ext[3]   // Extension
        size            // Size (in bytes)
        day             // Dia
        month           // Mes
        year            // Year
        hour            // Hour
        min             // Minute
        sec             // Second
        attrib          // Attributes
end

global struct video_modes[31]
        wide            // Mode width
        height          // Mode height
        mode            // Mode number
end

global timer[9]         // 10 millisecond counters for the user

global text_z=-256      // Print priority of the texts

global fading=0         // Tells whether a fade is in progress

global shift_status=0   // Actual shift status
global ascii=0          // Ascii code of last key pressed
global scan_code=0      // Scan code of last key pressed

global joy_filter=10    // Filter applied to the joystick (0..100%)
global joy_status=1     // Joystick state (0-off, 1-on, 2-forced)

global restore_type=1   // -1 Does not restore, 0 Partially, 1 Completely
global dump_type=1      // 0 Partial dump, 1 Full dump

global max_process_time=500 // Maximum execution time for a process

global fps=0            // Number of frames per second

global argc=0           // Number of parameters (minimum 1)
global argv[9]          // Pointers to the parameters (strings)

global channel[31]      // Information about the sound channels (1 if a sound was played)

global vsync=0          // Wait for the retrace (1-active, 0-inactive)

global draw_z=-255      // Print priority of the drawing primitives

global num_video_modes=0 // Number of video modes in struct video_modes[]

global unit_size=4      // Minimum word size for disk operations

//컴� Variables locales 컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴�

local struct reserved[0]
        process_id=0    // Process identifier
        id_scan=0       // To scan processes (collisions)
        process_type=0  // Process type
        type_scan=0     // To scan processes by type
        status=2        // Current state of this process
        parameters=0    // Number of parameters of the process
        param_offset=0  // Pointer to the passed parameters
        program_index=0 // Program counter for this process
        stack_pointer=0 // Stack pointer of the process
        is_executed=0   // Tells whether the process has already been executed
        is_painted=0    // Tells whether the process has already been drawn
        m8_object=-1    // Object inside the m8 world (Do not touch)
        old_ctype=0     // Old Ctype (Do not touch)
        frame_percent=0 // Percentage of frame elapsed
        box_x0=0        // Box occupied by the sprite each
        box_y0=0        //  time it is drawn, to perform
        box_x1=0        //  partial dump and background restore
        box_y1=0        //  partial (dump_type==partial_dump)
        f_count=0       // Function nesting counter
        caller_id=0     // Calling process or function (0 if it was the kernel)
end

local father=0          // Father identifier
local son=0             // Identifier of the last son
local smallbro=0        // Identifier of the younger brother
local bigbro=0          // Identifier of the older brother
local priority=0        // Process priority (higher is processed first)
local ctype=0           // Coordinate type
local x=0               // X coordinate
local y=0               // Y coordinate
local z=0               // Graphic print priority
local graph=0           // Graphic code for this process
local flags=0           // +1 horiz. flip, +2 vert. flip, +4 Ghost
local size=100          // Size of the process (as a percentage)
local angle=0           // Angle of the process
local region=0          // Clipping region for this process
local file=0            // File to take the graphics from
local xgraph=0          // Pointer to table: num_graphics, graph_angle_0, ...
local height=1          // Height of the processes in mode-7 (pix/4)
local cnumber=0         // Number of the scroll or m7 it is in (0 in all, or else: +1 in 0, +2 in 1, +4 in 2, ...)
local resolution=0      // Resolution of the x,y coordinates (0,10,100,...)

local radius=0          // Radius of the object in m8 (2...)
local m8_wall=-1        // Mode 8 wall it collides with
local m8_sector=-1      // Mode 8 sector it is in
local m8_nextsector=-1  // Mode 8 sector on the other side of the wall it collides with
local m8_step=32        // How much it can automatically climb in mode 8 when hitting a wall (step height)

